# GitHub — PR first, merge on GitHub only

When the user asks to **open a PR**, **merge**, or **finish GitHub-side** after a feature branch:

## What is forbidden

- **Do not** “finish” work by running `git checkout master`, `git merge <feature-branch>`, and `git push origin master` **instead of** opening a mergeable PR on GitHub. That bypasses the PR and is wrong unless the user **explicitly** asks for a **local merge without a PR** (rare).
- **Do not** treat a vague **“approved”** as permission to merge. Merge only after: the PR exists **and** either (a) the user approves/reviews on GitHub as your process requires, or (b) they send an explicit instruction such as **“merge the PR”** / **“merge to master”** referring to that PR.

## Auth (local)

- Root **`.env`** (gitignored) may define **`GITHUB_TOKEN`**. For **`gh`**, run `export GH_TOKEN="$GITHUB_TOKEN"` after sourcing `.env` in the same shell.
- For **`curl`** to `api.github.com`, use **`Authorization: Bearer $GITHUB_TOKEN`**. Never print tokens, commit them, or paste them into chat or logs.
- Tokens are **personal / dev-only**; do not put them in CI or shared config unless the user asks.

## Resolve `owner/repo`

From the repo root:

```bash
git remote get-url origin
```

Use `owner` and `repo` in API paths (e.g. `https://github.com/mmizin/CryptoSandboxQA` → `mmizin` / `CryptoSandboxQA`).

## Workflow order

1. **Push** the feature branch: `git push -u origin <branch>` (if not already pushed).
2. **Open a PR** targeting **`master`** with a clear title and short body:
   - **Prefer** `gh pr create --base master --head <branch> ...` when `gh` is installed and works.
   - **If `gh` is missing or broken**, create the PR with the **GitHub REST API** (do **not** stop at “here is the compare URL” when `GITHUB_TOKEN` is available in `.env`):

```bash
set -a && [ -f .env ] && . ./.env && set +a
# OWNER REPO from git remote, e.g. mmizin CryptoSandboxQA
curl -sS -X POST \
  -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${GITHUB_TOKEN}" \
  -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
  "https://api.github.com/repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls" \
  -d '{"title":"TITLE","head":"BRANCH","base":"master","body":"BODY"}'
```

3. **Stop** until merge is allowed (review / checks / explicit user instruction per team practice).
4. **Merge on GitHub** — not by local `git merge` into `master`:
   - **`gh pr merge`** (with `--delete-branch` if desired), or
   - **REST API:** `PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{pull_number}/merge` with the same auth headers.
5. **Local cleanup:** `git checkout master`, `git pull origin master`, `git branch -d <feature-branch>` (or `-D` only if the user confirms discarding an unmerged branch).

## If there is no token

If **`gh`** is unavailable **and** **`GITHUB_TOKEN`** is not loaded, say so and give the **compare URL**  
`https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/compare/master...<branch>`  
— still **do not** merge locally to `master` unless the user explicitly asks for that.

## Branch protection

If GitHub blocks merge (required reviews, failing checks), report it and wait; do not force-push around protection.
